        "evidence": "POST ResourceLibrary/GetLibraryDocuments URI/body parameter table (Tier 2)"
      }
    }
  },
  "WebhooksAvailable": false,
  "WebhooksNote": "No ''Webhook'' controller, and no webhook-registration operation of any kind, appears anywhere in the exhaustively-enumerated 236-operation / 25-controller catalog (scripts/enumerate-helppage.mjs). A confident-false, not an unprovable gap -- the API surface was fully enumerated, not merely sampled.",
  "BulkOperationsAvailable": false,
  "BulkOperationsNote": "No batch/bulk create-update-delete endpoint (a single request writing multiple records) is documented anywhere in the 236-operation catalog -- every write operation (PostToDiscussion, AddComment, Post/Edit Question, PostDocument, Ideation/Post, etc.) is single-record. Communities/GetCommunityMembers and DataFeed/GetData are BULK READS (many records per call), not bulk writes -- do not conflate. A confident-false based on exhaustive enumeration, not an unprovable gap.",
  "APIVersioningStrategy": "url-path",
  "APIVersioningNote": "Every one of the 236 documented operation paths is prefixed ''api/v2.0/...'' -- the API version is embedded directly in the URL path segment, confirmed uniformly across the entire enumerated catalog. No separate version header or query param is used anywhere.",
  "ErrorResponseShape": null,
  "ErrorResponseShapeNote": "UNDOCUMENTED. None of the 235 fetched op pages show an error-response sample (the HelpPage''s auto-generated ''Response Formats'' section documents only the SUCCESS shape). contextHLT.md''s own error-simulator section lists HTTP STATUS CODES to mock (400/401/403/404/409/422/429/500/503) but does not document a response BODY shape for any of them. Left null rather than guessed -- a genuine gap requiring either a live/sandbox error trigger or a support-ticket confirmation.",
  "CustomObjectMarkerPattern": null,
  "CustomObjectMarkerPatternNote": "No vendor-documented naming/prefix convention for customer-defined custom OBJECTS was found. Higher Logic Thrive Community''s extensibility surface (per this Tier-2 source) is expressed through first-class, dedicated object families -- Demographics (DemographicType/DemographicChoice, tenant-admin-configurable) and AutomationRules (tenant-configured rule schedules + a configurable fieldList) -- not through a dynamically-named custom-object family analogous to HubSpot''s p_<accountID>_<name>.",
  "CustomFieldMarkerPattern": null,
  "CustomFieldMarkerPatternNote": "No vendor-documented naming/prefix convention for customer-defined custom FIELDS on an existing object was found. The actual per-tenant custom-field extension points are (1) Demographics -- Demographics/GetDemographicTypes + GetDemographicChoices enumerate the CURRENT tenant''s configured custom demographic categories/choices attached to Contact, which a community admin can add/remove at any time (Demographics/AddDemographicCategory, AddDemographicChoice confirm these are admin-mutable) -- these are exposed as their OWN first-class DemographicType/DemographicChoice/ContactDemographic records, not as dynamically-named suffix/prefix fields on Contact''s schema; and (2) AutomationRules -- GetContactDataFields (`AvailableFields`) is itself a field-catalog/schema-introspection response for a rule''s configured Contact-data export, and GetContactData''s own `fieldList` parameter is tenant/rule-configured. Both extension points MUST flow through runtime discovery + the framework''s custom-column capture (see DiscoveryIsAuthoritative below), not a static naming-pattern marker.",
  "WriteCapability": {
    "supported": true,
    "scope": "Write endpoints exist for a MINORITY of the 34 taxonomy leaves. The remainder (Communities, CommunityMembers, CommunityInvitations, Contacts, Discussions[container]/DiscussionThreads, Events, EventTypes, EventSessions, RegistrantClasses, ResourceLibraryLibraries, DocumentAttachments(create/delete only, no update), DemographicTypes/Choices(create-only), Announcements, IdeaCategories(create-only)/IdeaStatuses, IdeaVoters, VolunteerOpportunities, VolunteerOpportunityTypes, Tags, AutomationRuleSchedules, AutomationRuleContactData, DataFeed) have NO write endpoint documented in the Community API v2.0 -- notably Contacts is written via the SEPARATE, out-of-scope Push API v2, NOT this API.",
    "create": "DiscussionPosts (PostToDiscussion / ReplyToDiscussion / PostToDiscussionWithCrossPost), Comments/BlogComments (Blogs/AddComment, ResourceLibrary/AddComment), Blogs (CreateBlog), Questions (Question/Post), Answers (Question/Answer), ResourceLibraryDocuments (PostDocument/libraryKey + a multipart-upload state machine: InitiateUpload -> MultipartUploaded/AbortMultipartUpload -> DocumentFromUpload), DocumentAttachments (PostDocumentAttachments), DemographicTypes/Choices (AddDemographicCategory / AddDemographicChoice -- create-only, no update/delete), Ideas (Ideation/Post), IdeaCategories (AddIdeaCategories -- create-only), Volunteers (VolunteerForOpportunity* by-key / by-legacy-key variants), ExternalActivity (ExternalActivity/Create -- the dedicated AMS-writeback object; ID location = response body, ExternalActivityKey echoed).",
    "update": "DiscussionPosts (PUT Discussions/Edit), Comments/BlogComments (Blogs/UpdateComment), Blogs (UpdateBlog, PublishBlog), Questions (Question/Edit), Answers (Answer/Edit), ResourceLibraryDocuments (ResourceLibrary/Edit), Ideas (Ideation/UpdateIdeaStatus), Volunteers (ApproveVolunteerApplication), ExternalActivity (PUT ExternalActivity/Update -- idiosyncratic: the key itself travels IN THE BODY, not as a URL path segment; ID location = body).",
    "delete": "DiscussionPosts (Discussions/RemovePost -- SEE DeleteSemanticsDetail: conditional soft-tombstone-vs-hard-delete), Blogs (DeleteBlog, DeleteComment, DeleteBlogRecommendation, DeleteRelatedLink), Questions (Question/Delete -- admin-only, cascades: all answers must be deleted first), Answers (Answer/Delete), ResourceLibraryDocuments (DeleteLibraryDocument, DeleteComment, DeleteDocumentRecommendation, DeleteRelatedLink), DocumentAttachments (DeleteDocumentAttachment), Volunteers (WithdrawFromOpportunity* by-key / by-legacy-key variants), ExternalActivity (Delete -- query-param ID location, not path).",
    "note": "Per-object write-surface detail (SupportsCreate/Update/Delete + Create/Update/DeleteAPIPath+Method+BodyShape+IDLocation) belongs on each IO row -- this is the Integration-level summary. ExternalActivity is the one genuinely WRITE-ONLY object (Create/Update/Delete exist; there is NO GET/list operation anywhere in the 236-op catalog) -- it is the vendor''s dedicated AMS-to-Community writeback channel, consistent with contextHLT.md''s framing.",
    "evidence": "SOURCE_STUDY.md ''Per-operation CRUD (write paths) confirmed for objects that have them'' table, derived from scripts/extract-op-details.mjs parsing of all 235 fetched op pages (Tier 2)."
  },
  "ConcurrencyControl": "none",
  "ConcurrencyControlNote": "No ETag, If-Match / If-Unmodified-Since header, or a version/revision field is documented on any Create/Update/Delete operation across the 236-operation catalog (confirmed by inspecting every write op''s URI+body parameter tables). Objects carry plain ''UpdatedOn''/''ModifiedOn''-style timestamp fields (informational provenance, not a concurrency-control mechanism -- no operation requires or accepts a matching version/etag value on write). Conflict resolution for any future bidirectional EntityMap must use snapshot-3-way only -- do not recommend MostRecent.",
  "DeleteSemantics": "hard",
  "DeleteSemanticsDetail": "The general pattern across write-capable leaves (Blogs/DeleteBlog, Question/Delete, Answer/Delete, ResourceLibrary/DeleteLibraryDocument, ResourceLibrary/DeleteDocumentAttachment, Volunteer/WithdrawFromOpportunity*, ExternalActivity/Delete) is a plain success response (''Resource Description: None'', typically 204 No Content) with NO soft-delete/archive flag or tombstone field documented on the corresponding model anywhere in this source -- treated as HARD delete per the honest-absence rule. ONE DOCUMENTED EXCEPTION: DELETE Discussions/RemovePost states verbatim ''Deletes the specified discussion post. If a message has replies, the body will be updated to: \"This post was removed\" and the message will be anonymized to preserve the thread structure. All documents attached to the message will be deleted.'' -- i.e. DiscussionPosts is CONDITIONALLY soft-tombstoned (body replaced + author anonymized) when the post has replies, and (implicitly) hard-deleted otherwise. This is a per-object exception the code-builder MUST encode on the DiscussionPosts IO specifically -- do not generalize it to other leaves, and do not treat the vendor-wide default as soft.",
  "DefaultSyncDirection": "Pull",
  "DefaultSyncDirectionNote": "Read-only default for every object per connector-code-conventions.md safety discipline, regardless of the substantial documented write surface on ~11 of 34 objects. Bidirectional sync requires sandbox validation first -- see BidirectionalPreconditions below.",
  "DefaultConflictResolution": "DestWins",
  "DefaultConflictResolutionReason": "ConcurrencyControl=none (no ETag/If-Match/version field documented anywhere in the 236-operation catalog) rules out MostRecent as a safe default -- MostRecent requires a reliable revision/timestamp-of-write signal to arbitrate conflicts, which the Community API v2.0 does not expose on any write operation. DestWins is the conservative default if/when any write-capable object (DiscussionPosts, Comments/BlogComments, Questions, Answers, ResourceLibraryDocuments, Ideas, Volunteers, ExternalActivity, Blogs) is ever enabled for bidirectional sync -- it overwrites the MJ destination with the vendor''s source-of-truth on pull, avoiding silent conflict-loss in either direction until a real concurrency signal is discovered.",
  "BidirectionalPreconditions": [
    "Obtain a live/sandbox Higher Logic Thrive Community tenant credential (IAM key/password) and empirically confirm the exact post-Login request-authorization header shape -- currently UNDOCUMENTED in every Tier 1/2/3 source collected during this research pass (see AuthHeaderPatternNote).",
    "Confirm whether the OIDC-API-auth alternative genuinely exists as a real machine-to-machine credential path -- currently a Tier-3-only, HelpPage-unconfirmed claim.",
    "Confirm real request/response shapes for each write-capable leaf (DiscussionPosts, Comments/BlogComments, Blogs, Questions, Answers, ResourceLibraryDocuments, Ideas, Volunteers, ExternalActivity) against a live/sandbox tenant -- currently known only from HelpPage-documented sample JSON, never from a live round-trip.",
    "Confirm the DiscussionPosts conditional soft-tombstone-vs-hard-delete behavior (RemovePost) against real production data BEFORE enabling delete-based sync on that object -- getting this wrong risks anonymizing/rewriting a real community member''s post content.",
    "Confirm no concurrency signal was missed on a live tenant (currently none documented anywhere) before ever recommending MostRecent conflict resolution.",
    "Confirm the true Token TTL/refresh behavior (currently UNDOCUMENTED) so long-running-sync retry/re-authentication semantics can be implemented correctly.",
    "Validate ALL write paths against a sandbox/test community BEFORE any bidirectional EntityMap touches a client''s real member/community/content data, per the read-first discipline -- must never be default-enabled."
  ],
  "RateLimitGuidance": {
    "guidance": "180-240 calls/minute (~3-4 requests/sec) acceptable-use guidance; NO hard server-enforced numeric rate limit or window is documented -- excessive usage risks IP blocking, not a deterministic 429.",
    "evidence": "support.higherlogic.com ''Higher Logic API'' article (Tier 2, HTTP-200-verified), per SOURCES.json: acceptable-use guidance only, explicitly stating no hard server-side rate-limit enforcement is documented.",
    "note": "Because this is GUIDANCE, not a stated precise numeric hard limit + window, Integration.BatchMaxRequestCount / BatchRequestWaitTime are left NULL per the provable-only discipline for hard-constraint Integration fields (a Tier-1/2 doc must state PRECISE limits; acceptable-use guidance with an explicit ''no hard limit documented'' caveat does not qualify). This note preserves the vendor''s own guidance so the code-builder can apply it as a conservative SELF-IMPOSED client-side throttle (e.g. target ~3 req/sec) even though it is not a metadata-enforced hard constraint."
  },
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamilies": [
    {
      "family": "Push API v2 (datapushapi.higherlogic.com/v2)",
      "reason": "Distinct host, distinct auth (Key header + ApiKey value), distinct direction (AMS/CRM pushes full-record-replacement data INTO the community, the inverse of this connector''s pull direction). A genuinely separate integration surface."
    },
    {
      "family": "ExternalSearch Add*Items (10 operations)",
      "reason": "Requires the separate External Search add-on plus a separate IAMKey, not available on a standard API v2.0 credential -- self-corroborated by the ExternalSearch controller''s own HelpPage description text."
    },
    {
      "family": "SSO (SAML / OIDC / OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code)",
      "reason": "End-user identity/login route (authorize/token/userinfo against an external IdP), not a data-sync route; no relationship to the Community API v2.0 object model."
    },
    {
      "family": "Messaging (private inbox/sent messages)",
      "reason": "Private user-to-user direct messages -- not organizational/member data an AMS/CRM sync connector targets; judgment call per task instruction."
    },
    {
      "family": "Friends (social-graph friend requests)",
      "reason": "Member-to-member social connection graph, not organizational membership/engagement data; judgment call per task instruction."
    },
    {
      "family": "Federation (cross-tenant identity)",
      "reason": "Federates identity across separate Higher Logic communities -- not applicable to a single-tenant AMS/CRM connector; judgment call per task instruction."
    }
  ],
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamiliesRationale": "All 6 families are genuine record/operation types the HelpPage PROVES exist (not fabricated) but were judged out of scope for an AMS/CRM sync connector -- see SOURCE_STUDY.md section 4/5 for full per-family evidence (Push API v2 confirmed via support.higherlogic.com ''Higher Logic Push API v2'' article, Tier 2; ExternalSearch self-corroborated by the HelpPage''s own ExternalSearch controller description text; SSO confirmed via the ''OAuth 2.0 Code Flow'' support article, Tier 2; Messaging/Friends/Federation are HelpPage-proven controllers excluded by scope judgment, not by missing evidence).",
  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritative": false,
  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritativeRationale": "Set to FALSE (the conservative/safe default). There is NO complete-gamut ''describe my full schema'' endpoint anywhere in the 236-operation catalog. GET System/GetApiDetails enumerates CONTROLLERS+OPERATIONS (the RPC surface itself -- Name/Endpoints/Parameters), NOT a data-object field schema, and it is not scoped to what a given IAM credential can access -- it appears to be a static reflection of the whole deployed API regardless of caller identity/entitlements (no evidence it varies per-credential). Two genuinely per-tenant, credential-gated extension points exist and MUST flow through runtime discovery + the framework''s custom-column capture rather than being frozen as static metadata: (1) Demographics -- GetDemographicTypes/GetDemographicChoices enumerate the CURRENT tenant''s configured custom demographic fields/categories, which differ per community and are admin-mutable at any time (AddDemographicCategory/AddDemographicChoice confirm mutability); (2) AutomationRules -- GetContactDataFields (''AvailableFields'') is itself a field-catalog/schema-introspection response for a given automation rule''s configured Contact-data export, and GetContactData''s own ''fieldList'' parameter is tenant/rule-configured, not a fixed vendor set. Because neither of these -- nor any other object -- has a describe endpoint proven to return the COMPLETE gamut a credential can access, DiscoveryIsAuthoritative stays at its conservative default; absence-on-a-later-refresh must NOT be treated as authoritative proof of removal for this connector.",
  "AdditionalObservations": [
    {
      "Key": "VendorDocGenerationBug",
      "Value": "Events/GetEvent, Events/GetEventType, GetEventTypes, GetEventTypesList, SaveEventType, DeleteEventType, RestoreEventType, and RegistrantClass/GetRegistrantClasses all document their Resource Description as the raw ASP.NET HttpResponseMessage envelope instead of the real typed model, and carry no sample JSON -- confirmed real vendor doc-generation breakage (not an access restriction; the working Events/GetUpcoming/SearchEvents/etc. operations DO show the real 76-field Event model).",
      "Provenance": "SOURCE_STUDY.md Patterns and Motifs #4 (Tier 2)"
    },
    {
      "Key": "OneUnreachableOpPage",
      "Value": "GET Discussions/GetLatestTopics returns a persistent vendor-side HTTP 500 (2 attempts confirmed) -- a vendor doc-page bug, not an access block; equivalent discussion-topic data is reachable via GetRecentThreads/GetSubscribedDiscussions.",
      "Provenance": "SOURCE_STUDY.md section 6 gap #7 (Tier 2, this agent''s own source-collection run)"
    },
    {
      "Key": "MisleadingSupportArticleTitle",
      "Value": "support.higherlogic.com article 360033049191 (''API General Information'') actually documents Thrive MARKETING''s legacy ActionRequest/GridRequest XML web service (username+password+BrandID auth), NOT the Community API v2.0 -- a documented vendor-doc-organization pitfall; not cited as evidence for any Community API v2.0 claim in this file.",
      "Provenance": "SOURCES.json entry for that URL (Tier 3, flagged pitfall)"
    }
  ]
}' EXEC [__mj].spCreateIntegration @Name = @Name_37afcc56,
  @Description = @Description_37afcc56,
  @NavigationBaseURL = @NavigationBaseURL_37afcc56,
  @ClassName = @ClassName_37afcc56,
  @ImportPath = @ImportPath_37afcc56,
  @BatchMaxRequestCount = @BatchMaxRequestCount_37afcc56,
  @BatchRequestWaitTime = @BatchRequestWaitTime_37afcc56,
  @ID = @ID_37afcc56,
  @CredentialTypeID = @CredentialTypeID_37afcc56,
  @Icon = @Icon_37afcc56,
  @Configuration = @Configuration_37afcc56;

GO

